+The Lean~4 development for Sections~\ref{sec:random_walks}--\ref{sec:percolation} is available at \url{https://github.com/Nero-17/LEAN-Formalisation-IGS-RWDL}.
+The initial development used Aristotle (Harmonic) \cite{achim2025aristotle}; subsequent extensions construct the actual graph, measure, energy and process objects required by the statements below.
+For the verified interfaces, the proofs contain no \texttt{sorry}, no \texttt{admit} and no additional mathematical \texttt{axiom}; their printed dependencies are contained in \texttt{propext}, \texttt{Classical.choice} and \texttt{Quot.sound}.
+
+The actual-model interfaces derive their conclusions from the finite substitution rules under the standing hypotheses, or under the separate assumptions of a worked example.
+In particular, the metric limit, closed energy form, limiting process and heat kernel are constructed within the development, rather than supplied as hypotheses asserting the corresponding conclusions.
+The resistance-form identification retains the condition $\rho(\Psi)>1$.
+The random-geometric and diffusion predictions in the Outlook remain conjectures, and the DHL logarithmic sharpness assertion concerns the volume upper bound only.
+Table~\ref{tab:lean} summarises these interfaces; the repository records exact source hashes and compiler receipts separately from exploratory candidates.
+The presence of a candidate source file is not a verification claim.
 
